View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really really niche, but I've been thinking a lot about a &quot;Satanic Panic&quot; Beast period. Set in 80s and early 90s rural Americana and inspired by such scandals and modern day witch hunts as the Frankin Coverup, the McMartin Preschool case and the West Memphis 3. Maybe a 2nd edition update for Possessed as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T21:00:13-07:00","id":949791,"title":"","content":"Whch gameline do you think fits the Spanish Civil War best? A doomed power play by the Carthians seems a little too on the nose, but I'm having a hard time thinking of something more poetic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:46:34-07:00","id":949896,"title":"","content":"I think Uxas suggested Geist for that period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-12T23:54:23-07:00","id":949899,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I suggested Geist. I also think Vampire eould be a great option, with s shadow war of Carthians against Invictus and Sanctified.<br /> <br /> But if I had to choose one, I think Geist is more appropiated in theme and mood.<br /> <br /> In fact, i have ideas for vampire, werewolf, mage and geist for Spanish Civil War, although the only ones I have more or less developed are vampire and werewolf","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 08-13-2016, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:03:08-07:00","id":949908,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a nicely crafted werewolf and vampire setting with alliances, politicking and internal conflict and both dealing with external enemies on top of all that.<br /> <br /> It overlaps too much with classic, and is overdone in general, but the Crusades keep coming to mind. Perhaps colonial Mexico. You have silver mines and slavery. Depending on when it happened you had a more peaceful and successful religious conversion of natives and slavery being outlawed by the mendicant orders. Or later on the vicious Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-13-2016, 03:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T00:11:41-07:00","id":949913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=949899#post949899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah. I suggested Geist. I also think Vampire eould be a great option, with s shadow war of Carthians against Invictus and Sanctified.<br /> <br /> But if I had to choose one, I think Geist is more appropiated in theme and mood.<br /> <br /> In fact, i have ideas for vampire, werewolf, mage and geist for Spanish Civil War, although the only ones I have more or less developed are vampire and werewolf</div> </div> </div> </div>Could be interesting to see Geist's &quot;second chance&quot; thing applied less to the joy of life and more about sacrificing everything for a cause because you want your death to mean something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T11:11:09-07:00","id":950153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=948941#post948941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really really niche, but I've been thinking a lot about a &quot;Satanic Panic&quot; Beast period. Set in 80s and early 90s rural Americana and inspired by such scandals and modern day witch hunts as the Frankin Coverup, the McMartin Preschool case and the West Memphis 3. Maybe a 2nd edition update for Possessed as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have done a lot of research on the satanic panic for my novel series (Thee first few books of the series in the 80s story arc are basically an ace attorney tribute based around the Satanic Panic). This dark era should make sure to mention the conspiracy theories that the panic itself was the work of a group or groups that wanted to distract and/or trick the faithful. For example, there are lot of people who think the panic was intentionally started by the catholic church (remember that the guy who wrote the book Michelle Remembers and lit the fuse on the panic by doing so had connection to the Vatican) to cover up their child abuse. So, having some MM hunters on the run from their conspiracy because they know too much and are willing to help the Beast PCs in exchange for protection in that might be cool.<br /> <br /> One personal theory of mine is that Phill Phillips (the Turmoil in the Toybox guy) was a puppet of a group that took advantage of the satanic panic to give children a bad image of Christianity that would lead to them leaving the faith by associating Christianity with mean people who broke and burned their toys (the so-called Operation Bad Santa)<br /> <br /> Also, there should a few winks and nods to the cWod in this dark era, since many of the creators of the cWoD were raised by families who believed in that satanic panic stuff, which then influenced the CwoD.<br /> <br /> Also, keep in mind that trashy talk show hosts played an important role in spreading the panic. Also keep in mind that a Beast who went after Oprah for that could easily gorge themselves on her phobia of chewing gum.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh one more thing, while most people think of fundamentalists as being the main satanic panicers, many people forget that the 2nd wave feminist movement also bought into it on the preventing child abuse angle. Here is an <a href=\"http://www.spiked-online.com/newsite/article/13119#.V69lSjVe_uc\" target=\"_blank\">article </a>on the role 2nd wave feminism played in that witch hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-13-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T17:56:22-07:00","id":950336,"title":"","content":"I'm...not sure it's a good idea to explore things in ChroD through that sort of polemical lens. Trying to use a tabletop roleplaying game to convince people that a historical event was an atheist/catholic scheme to drive kids away from christianity is....not the best idea. But for me, the greater danger in using the Satanic Panic in a game about monsters is that you risk validating it. In the real world, the Panic was a tragic clusterfuck because there aren't actually demon-worshipping murdercults kidnapping children and brainwashing people. In ChroD, there kind of are. So if you put that era into ChroD, you risk making it seem like the Panic-ers had a point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T18:59:15-07:00","id":950368,"title":"","content":"Because I can't just passively upvote them, I'm going to have to agree with Gecko, especially since such things are so close to living memory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:01:35-07:00","id":950371,"title":"","content":", or mn<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950336#post950336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm...not sure it's a good idea to explore things in ChroD through that sort of polemical lens. Trying to use a tabletop roleplaying game to convince people that a historical event was an atheist/catholic scheme to drive kids away from christianity is....not the best idea. But for me, the greater danger in using the Satanic Panic in a game about monsters is that you risk validating it. In the real world, the Panic was a tragic clusterfuck because there aren't actually demon-worshipping murdercults kidnapping children and brainwashing people. In ChroD, there kind of are. So if you put that era into ChroD, you risk making it seem like the Panic-ers had a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite what I was saying ( I was saying the Catholics made it up as a diversion and then other groups took advantage of the panic for their own ends, with no abuse or anything like that actually happening. Basically the idea being that the panic was bullshit even in the CofD, but that certain groups took advantage of the fear itself.) But I get what you are saying, maybe in a few decades when it is further behind us, or maybe even just portray the panic as a wholly mundane evil, with the monsters purely as bystanders, profiteers, victims and sometimes, against all odds, heroes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-13-2016, 10:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:08:50-07:00","id":950375,"title":"","content":"There's no reason to avoid conspiracy theories, though. More specifically, people believing them, even if they're wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:12:55-07:00","id":950376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950375#post950375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no reason to avoid conspiracy theories, though. More specifically, people believing them, even if they're wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Having some Null Mysterius fellow who accuses the Catholic church of starting the panic to cover Catholic abuse f children would work, even if having it being confirmed truth is out of bounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:15:53-07:00","id":950377,"title":"","content":"I still want my Weimar Republic Werewolf/Changeling/Geist clusterfuck. This has not changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:16:36-07:00","id":950378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The young man in the cafe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950376#post950376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fair enough. Having some Null Mysterius fellow who accuses the Catholic church of starting the panic to cover Catholic abuse f children would work, even if having it being confirmed truth is out of bounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like this a lot. As a survivor, I find it cathartic to examine those kinds of topics as long as they're handled well. But I don't see it happening. Don't hold me to this, for all I know, I'll be proven wrong, but in my experience so far writing for the company, we've started trying to avoid rape and abuse more and more. <br /> <br /> Again, don't hold me to that, I'm not the one who decides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:24:00-07:00","id":950382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950378#post950378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would like this a lot. As a survivor, I find it cathartic to examine those kinds of topics as long as they're handled well. But I don't see it happening. Don't hold me to this, for all I know, I'll be proven wrong, but in my experience so far writing for the company, we've started trying to avoid rape and abuse more and more.<br /> <br /> Again, don't hold me to that, I'm not the one who decides.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. And that reminds me that one thing that should absolutely be mentioned by the Dark Era if it gets made is that the hyper-focus on the non-existent SRA resulted in the more mundane evil of incest type abuse being more or less ignored by the authorities. The whole theme of this Dark Era is that sometimes humans are their own monsters and the worst evil is completely non-supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T19:49:22-07:00","id":950390,"title":"","content":"Hm... well, these are just a few thoughts, but: <br /> <br /> 1. Crusades. Vampire could be fertile ground to explore, since it had a chapter in Ancient Bloodlines/Mysteries focussing on the Middle Ages; the Lancea et Sanctum using the Crusades as cover to go after non-Sanctified vampires could also be an interesting angle. Mages could also be interesting, with the East-meets-West dynamic of Alexander's conquests in &quot;To the Strongest&quot; getting echoed, and some mages wondering if a new paradigm shift in Awakened society is coming. A hunter setting with Hunter-on-Hunter action due to the confusion of religion and politics, while the monsters go unfought, could be interesting as well. <br /> <br /> 2. Renaissance Italy. Vampire all the way. The debauchery, the intrigue, the juxtaposition of humanism and religion, republicanism and despotism. A Methuselah Embraced before the Western Empire fell feels genuine joy for the first time in centuries as he watches Italy return to her former glory... an elder who entered Torpor after the Camarilla fell awakens to find the Invictus has essentially replaced it. <br /> <br /> 3. Golden Age of Piracy. Mage could be interesting, perhaps with a proto-Free Council Nameless Order mirroring the Pirate Republic of Nassau, and European mages coming into contact with American Awakened and comparing notes. Werewolf could be cool, because &quot;werewolf pirates&quot; just sounds like an inherently awesome premise. Sin-Eaters could be fun too, and I think others have echoed similar sentiments. <br /> <br /> 4. Seven Year's War/American War of Independence. Maybe see where Hunters stand after &quot;Doubting Souls,&quot; or explore how the interplay between European and Native werewolves turned out, plus the fact that a lot of battles were fought on the frontier sounds like werewolves could be in their element on either side of the fight. <br /> <br /> 5. French Revolution. Especially picking up where &quot;Lily, Saber and Thorn&quot; left off, and see how things have changed for the French Changelings. Beast could also be appropriate, because they didn't call it the &quot;Terror&quot; for nothing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:07:12-07:00","id":950393,"title":"","content":"I know there is something Mage could do with the dotcom bubble of the late 90s, between the dreams of tech utopia that didn't pan out, the sheer hubris of the dotcom executives mirroring the disasters hubris can cause for magi, I just know that some good stories could come of that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T20:51:04-07:00","id":950419,"title":"","content":"Regarding Satanic Panic Beast; It is something that has happened in recent memory and many of the people involved are still alive and had their lives ruined from the accusations. It would require a great deal of respect, research, and tact to pull of right. Something I know Onyx Path is capable of but I can absolutely understand why it would turn people off. <br /> <br /> On a lighter note, I would like Bronze Age Greece Hunter/Beast and a Weimar Republic crossover sounds fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11643-corax","name":"Corax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:43:11-07:00","id":950433,"title":"","content":"I'd kill for Renaissance Italy Demon, with clockwork demons leaping from Da Vinci's pages and scheming with th best in Venice or Rome, all under the watchful eye of a Catholic church that sometimes has some distinctly unholy gears turning behind the scenes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-13T21:46:58-07:00","id":950434,"title":"","content":"The Taiping Rebellion (Vampire and Werewolf) - China is dominated by a calcified Confucian Covenant, deathless elders even more resistant to change than the decaying dynasty they help to prop up. Try as they might to stamp out the encroaching infestation of European Kindred they keep coming: the Invictus with their fingers in colonial interests, the Lancea following the spread of the missionaries, the Ordo seeking to plunder hidden knowledge. Vampires were not behind the Taiping revolt, but they did seek to exploit it. The Lancea in particular latched on to the Taipings' peculiar brand of Christianity and sought to make them their proxies. They failed, instead spawning an aggressive movement of Taiping Kindred that expand rapidly and gruesomely dispatch Confucian and European alike. The Confucians entrench themselves in palaces of shadow and gardens of smoke, obsessively playing out pomp and ritual that increasingly has no meaning, while the Europeans barricade themselves in colonial enclaves and gorge themselves on the excesses of empire. Outside blood runs aplenty and plague ravages those not cut down by war. <br /> <br /> To the Uratha one thing is obvious, the world is not in harmony. Things could hardly be more terribly unbalanced. Natural disasters strike with ominous frequency, the Yellow River floods so severely that its course is altered by hundreds of miles, famine and disease are rampant, law and order are absent or impotent. Contact with Europe has brought new ideas, new technology, and new problems, whether they want them or not. The natural, cultural, and spiritual worlds are in chaos. It all seems too much, too vast, and though the Uratha have to will to put it right they lack the unity. Some believe in expelling all intrusive influences and returning to a state of purity. Others contend that the only salvation is through adaptation, taming the storm by force and with new visions. Both are divided within themselves over whether the old leadership must be preserved at all costs, or removed by any means necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T05:46:47-07:00","id":950516,"title":"","content":"I'd like an Inferno dark era, I'm not sure which era works best for it though. Prohibition Chicago? The founding of Las Vegas as a gambling city? 80s Wall Street? Hollywood?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want it to be too on the nose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T06:09:39-07:00","id":950522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950516#post950516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd like an Inferno dark era, I'm not sure which era works best for it though. Prohibition Chicago? The founding of Las Vegas as a gambling city? 80s Wall Street? Hollywood?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want it to be too on the nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've suggested the Italian Renaissance because its theme of &quot;rebirth from the dark age&quot;- after centuries of ignorance and fear, which well fed the fires of Inferno, now starts a new time as the world reclaim itself from the hold of Hell (need some work in order to avoid &quot;the Church is evil&quot; theme- probably by using Inferno as a scavenger which exploit existing corruption and revels in rot). Crossing it together with Descent Demons, as atamajakki suggested, could make a very interesting and fully demonic Era- themes of reclaiming former glory and rebuilding from corrupted elements. One kind of demons tries to pulls the world back to one Hell, the other works to move it forward a new one. A lot of potential for backstabbing, manipulation and espionage as the demons fight over the souls of the people trapped in the middle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T09:22:38-07:00","id":950589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Corax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950419#post950419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Satanic Panic Beast; It is something that has happened in recent memory and many of the people involved are still alive and had their lives ruined from the accusations. It would require a great deal of respect, research, and tact to pull of right. Something I know Onyx Path is capable of but I can absolutely understand why it would turn people off.<br /> <br /> On a lighter note, I would like Bronze Age Greece Hunter/Beast and a Weimar Republic crossover sounds fascinating.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, which is actually part of why it would be important to do this, in a way. The sad fact is, many modern portrayals of the satanic panic play that whole vile chapter of American history for laughs, forgetting that real people had their lives ruined by it. To quote the main character of the Marvels miniseries, &quot;What were they thinking? You could see it in their faces, they weren't thinking. They were just afraid and angry, and they were lashing out. And when they woke up tomorrow morning. It would just be a dream. Something that happened to someone else. I had to get a record... had to show them.. show us all... what we did in out nightmare.&quot; The point being is that as much as the American public may want to forget the horrors of the panic, we can't let them .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T13:36:10-07:00","id":950724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950377#post950377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still want my Weimar Republic Werewolf/Changeling/Geist clusterfuck. This has not changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify:<br /> <br /> For <b>Werewolf</b> you have the <i>freikorps</i> and the (sometimes violent) politics -as one of my professors once put it, it was a democracy run by people who didn't want a democracy for people who didn't want a democracy. You have that whole aspect of Germany <i>losing a war</i> for the first time to play with. And I don't doubt that the Shadow would be... interesting.<br /> <br /> For <b>Changeling</b>, you have the whole hyperliberalism of the Weimar period. Prostitution and homosexuality were <i>legal</i>, and women had the vote (almost 2 years before the US). There's a <i>wild</i> backlash in the art and nascent film movements that oppose the naturalism of their predecessors, and philosophy is all over the place. Juxtapose that with the atmosphere of poverty, shame, and anger that ultimately led to the Third Reich, and you've got an interesting backdrop for Changelings.<br /> <br /> For <b>Geist</b>... a juxtaposition of the beginning (WWI and the Spanish Flu) and the end (Reichsmordwoche, Kristallnacht, and the rest of the rise of the Nazi party). That's all I need to say, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:46:02-07:00","id":950758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950724#post950724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To clarify:<br /> <br /> For <b>Werewolf</b> you have the <i>freikorps</i> and the (sometimes violent) politics -as one of my professors once put it, it was a democracy run by people who didn't want a democracy for people who didn't want a democracy. You have that whole aspect of Germany <i>losing a war</i> for the first time to play with. And I don't doubt that the Shadow would be... interesting.<br /> <br /> For <b>Changeling</b>, you have the whole hyperliberalism of the Weimar period. Prostitution and homosexuality were <i>legal</i>, and women had the vote (almost 2 years before the US). There's a <i>wild</i> backlash in the art and nascent film movements that oppose the naturalism of their predecessors, and philosophy is all over the place. Juxtapose that with the atmosphere of poverty, shame, and anger that ultimately led to the Third Reich, and you've got an interesting backdrop for Changelings.<br /> <br /> For <b>Geist</b>... a juxtaposition of the beginning (WWI and the Spanish Flu) and the end (Reichsmordwoche, Kristallnacht, and the rest of the rise of the Nazi party). That's all I need to say, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've sold me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T14:57:16-07:00","id":950760,"title":"","content":"I still really want to do Mummy: Infinite Macabre, in 19,544 CE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T15:10:47-07:00","id":950768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950760#post950760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still really want to do Mummy: Infinite Macabre, in 19,544 CE.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no. Anything but new Mummy content to fill the void that will fill the next year or two!<br /> <br /> I'd love to see that. The little bit of info in Book of the Deceived about the Sothic Turn on Mars after mankind has died off was awesome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T23:01:29-07:00","id":950942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950516#post950516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd like an Inferno dark era, I'm not sure which era works best for it though. Prohibition Chicago? The founding of Las Vegas as a gambling city? 80s Wall Street? Hollywood?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't want it to be too on the nose.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've personally been chewing on Old Shanghai for an Inferno-centric era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T23:44:24-07:00","id":950953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950760#post950760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still really want to do Mummy: Infinite Macabre, in 19,544 CE.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Has WoD ever gone into the future? I have always wanted to do a blue book game somewhere between Alien and Outland (the Sean Connery sci-fi where he doesn't wear a read loincloth...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5622-sprucestripedgoose","name":"SpruceStripedGoose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5622_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-14T23:46:28-07:00","id":950954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr Innes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950942#post950942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've personally been chewing on Old Shanghai for an Inferno-centric era.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whenever anyone asks me what settings I think deserve more love, I always suggest Victorian Hong Kong and 1930s Shanghai. Both are so worthy of love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T02:05:45-07:00","id":950985,"title":"","content":"I'd love to pitch Industrial Revolution Demon/Promethean, with the focus on the God-Machine encouraging a mechanised society (with a central question of <i>why </i>and why <i>now</i>) while the economic and social ramifications, including mass migration to squalid cities, make wonderful grist for Prometheans.<br /> <br /> Picture Demonic Luddites smashing machines, Promethean factory-workers and miners, games that follow the rise of unions (which can easily feed into both gamelines), environmental damage easily conflated with Wastelands... The Unfleshed would naturally get a lot of love, but you could potentially create a lineage of Prometheans made from human bodies but with Oil as their humour...<br /> <br /> I'd probably set in it in Birmingham, a key center for the industrial revolution's scientific, industrial and social aspects with a lot of immigration from around the world, allowing a lot of variety for player characters (and I could have a lot of fun with the Lunar Society). Though Peaky Blinders is later, the show's popularity might help :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 08-15-2016, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T04:03:28-07:00","id":951032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SpruceStripedGoose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950953#post950953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Has WoD ever gone into the future? I have always wanted to do a blue book game somewhere between Alien and Outland (the Sean Connery sci-fi where he doesn't wear a read loincloth...)</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a <i>Mirrors </i>supplement! Actually getting ready to run a future game myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T06:37:26-07:00","id":951071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=950724#post950724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To clarify:<br /> <br /> For <b>Werewolf</b> you have the <i>freikorps</i> and the (sometimes violent) politics -as one of my professors once put it, it was a democracy run by people who didn't want a democracy for people who didn't want a democracy. You have that whole aspect of Germany <i>losing a war</i> for the first time to play with. And I don't doubt that the Shadow would be... interesting.<br /> <br /> For <b>Changeling</b>, you have the whole hyperliberalism of the Weimar period. Prostitution and homosexuality were <i>legal</i>, and women had the vote (almost 2 years before the US). There's a <i>wild</i> backlash in the art and nascent film movements that oppose the naturalism of their predecessors, and philosophy is all over the place. Juxtapose that with the atmosphere of poverty, shame, and anger that ultimately led to the Third Reich, and you've got an interesting backdrop for Changelings.<br /> <br /> For <b>Geist</b>... a juxtaposition of the beginning (WWI and the Spanish Flu) and the end (Reichsmordwoche, Kristallnacht, and the rest of the rise of the Nazi party). That's all I need to say, really.</div> </div> </div> </div>And then the sobering thought that any nonsense perpetrated by these splats is going to pale in comparison to a horror the world as never seen before...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 08-15-2016, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:18:11-07:00","id":951116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951071#post951071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then the sobering thought that any nonsense perpetrated by these splats is going to end in a horror the world as never seen before...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more sobering when you consider that there's nothing they can do to <i>stop</i> it. I would certainly have the chapter end before the actual abolishment of democracy - that's the part of history that everyone remembers. Because if it got to that point...<br /> <br /> That's a different period altogether. And it'd have to be Beast - and would be one of the reasons that I <i>hate</i> Beast. <i>That's</i> what happens when large masses of people are frightened, you <i>idiots</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:25:23-07:00","id":951120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951071#post951071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And then the sobering thought that any nonsense perpetrated by these splats is going to end in a horror the world as never seen before...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be leery of ascribing too much supernatural influence to the rise of the Nazis. That's something that the Worlds of Darkness have generally steered clear from throughout their publishing history, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> That being said, a Weimar setting seems like an excellent era to include Hunter in through the Thule Gesellschaft and the Loyalist schism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:28:06-07:00","id":951124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951116#post951116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's more sobering when you consider that there's nothing they can do to <i>stop</i> it. I would certainly have the chapter end before the actual abolishment of democracy - that's the part of history that everyone remembers. Because if it got to that point...<br /> <br /> That's a different period altogether. And it'd have to be Beast - and would be one of the reasons that I <i>hate</i> Beast. <i>That's</i> what happens when large masses of people are frightened, you <i>idiots</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue that the Holocaust is an example of the horror of moral apathy than an example of the horror of mass panic. People knew what was going on and turned a blind eye, or knew &quot;something&quot; was going on and decided they were better off ignoring the big, terrible thing that was happening just over the hill, but at least they had enough plausible deniability to rationalize their inaction. The rise of Nazism had more to do with Hitler playing on Germans' frustration and shame than their fear. <br /> <br /> Beast, to me, is more early Cold War, with nuclear panic and Communist paranoia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:34:42-07:00","id":951128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951120#post951120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be leery of ascribing too much supernatural influence to the rise of the Nazis. That's something that the Worlds of Darkness have generally steered clear from throughout their publishing history, for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> That being said, a Weimar setting seems like an excellent era to include Hunter in through the Thule Gesellschaft and the Loyalist schism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant to type that their actions are going to pale in comparison to the Nazis' actions. I went back and realized that I had ascribed supernatural origins and motivation to the Nazi atrocities. To me, it basically hand waves human moral culpability and ignores the human potential for evil by blaming a supernatural force. It's a more elaborate version of &quot;The Devil made me do it.&quot; Saying stuff like &quot;The Holocaust was a God-Machine operation&quot; or such nonsense is really tasteless in my book, and I would rather avoid it. If Onyx Path could sit down and discuss how the various splats react to the horror in a mature way it could be interesting, but please, don't have some vampire Elders be the ones who cooked up the Final Solution.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 08-15-2016, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T08:43:19-07:00","id":951134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951128#post951128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant to type that their actions is going to pale in comparison to the Nazis' actions. I went back and realized that I had ascribed supernatural origins and motivation to the Nazi atrocities. To me, it basically hand waves human moral culpability and ignores the human potential for evil by blaming a supernatural force. It's a more elaborate version of &quot;The Devil made me do it.&quot; Saying stuff like &quot;The Holocaust was a God-Machine operation&quot; or such nonsense is really tasteless in my book, and I would rather avoid it. If Onyx Path could sit down and discuss how the various splats react to the horror in a mature way could be interesting, but please, don't have some vampire Elders be the ones who cooked up the Final Solution.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully I don't think that would be likely. Keeping the Holocaust an entirely human atrocity has been the standing policy pretty much from the beginning, and I think everyone agrees its the best way to handle it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: With one notable exception that shall not be named. <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*cough* Vampire Himmler *cough*</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","user":"Caitiff Primogen","date":". 08-15-2016, 11:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T10:16:40-07:00","id":951182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951134#post951134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thankfully I don't think that would be likely. Keeping the Holocaust an entirely human atrocity has been the standing policy pretty much from the beginning, and I think everyone agrees its the best way to handle it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: With one notable exception that shall not be named. <span style=\"font-size:10px\">*cough* Vampire Himmler *cough*</span></div> </div> </div> </div>White Wolf made some <i>interesting </i>choices back in the day...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:02:52-07:00","id":951206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=948132#post948132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No mummy was actually awake and active during the period immediately following the fall of Irem, so it's actually not all that interesting to place a Mummy Era in it. They don't wake up until roughly 1.5 thousand years after the fall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Came upon this by Mr. Brookshaw:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The shan'iatu performed the Rite of Return in 3832 BCE - it's not 6000 BCE, it's 6000 *years ago*. </div> </div> </div>That's kind of spot-on for the era I was thinking of. Again, I haven't read any of the Mummy stuff myself. How feasible would a Mummy game be for the period of their initial creation? I'm tempted to buy the book just so I can flesh out the idea and pitch it. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T11:41:38-07:00","id":951220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951206#post951206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Came upon this by Mr. Brookshaw:<br /> <br /> <br /> That's kind of spot-on for the era I was thinking of. Again, I haven't read any of the Mummy stuff myself. How feasible would a Mummy game be for the period of their initial creation? I'm tempted to buy the book just so I can flesh out the idea and pitch it. :-)</div> </div> </div> </div>First of all, Mummy is probably my favorite CofD gameline and I suggest you definitely give it a look; you'll either love it, hate it, or be like me and hate it until you figure things out and then love it.<br /> <br /> The long and short of things is the era you're looking at is during the existence of the Nameless Empire, a predynastic Egyptian civilization centered on the lost city of Irem that was ruled by inhuman necromancer-priests called the Shan'iatu. All of the mummies would still be alive as mortal human beings in their Guilds, practicing their sacred crafts until they're ritually murdered by the Shan'iatu. Things get a little weird because they they stay dead for another 1400 years, so a Mummy setting at the time would just be a mortals game in a lost semi-mythic Bronze Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:08:15-07:00","id":951264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951220#post951220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, Mummy is probably my favorite CofD gameline and I suggest you definitely give it a look; you'll either love it, hate it, or be like me and hate it until you figure things out and then love it.<br /> <br /> The long and short of things is the era you're looking at is during the existence of the Nameless Empire, a predynastic Egyptian civilization centered on the lost city of Irem that was ruled by inhuman necromancer-priests called the Shan'iatu. All of the mummies would still be alive as mortal human beings in their Guilds, practicing their sacred crafts until they're ritually murdered by the Shan'iatu. Things get a little weird because they they stay dead for another 1400 years, so a Mummy setting at the time would just be a mortals game in a lost semi-mythic Bronze Age.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless if gave us rules for Sekhem Sorcerers and sacred geometry, in which case the fan base may lose their minds, as those rules could still be relevant in modern games. It could be a really cool Second Sight era that used Mummy's backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T13:09:35-07:00","id":951265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951264#post951264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unless if gave us rules for Sekhem Sorcerers and sacred geometry, in which case the fan base may lose their minds, as those rules could still be relevant in modern games. It could be a really cool Second Sight era that used Mummy's backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sekhem sorcery is supposed to be in the Cleopatra setting in the Companion, and hopefully relic architecture will either be in the Mutapa setting or Rio.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T14:00:56-07:00","id":951301,"title":"","content":"One I'd like to see is 1950's-60's Japan for Beast.<br /> <br /> This was the time of the Kaiju Golden Age for Japan. Which of course the first kaiju movie Godzilla (1954) was a metaphor for unchecked nuclear devastation. And in the early years, was back when kaiju movies were made with the intent of being scary. Which in of itself could be used to look at Japan as they were dealing with all the fallout from the end of WWII (the American occupation, shift in government, and an even further Westernization of their culture). And the 60's also oversaw the creation of tokusatsu heroes like Ultraman, with an actual Hero rising to fight giant monsters (which could lead into the 70's and how that was the Golden Age of heroes for Japan with guys like Kamen Rider and Super Sentai).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T17:13:24-07:00","id":951389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951301#post951301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One I'd like to see is 1950's-60's Japan for Beast.<br /> <br /> This was the time of the Kaiju Golden Age for Japan. Which of course the first kaiju movie Godzilla (1954) was a metaphor for unchecked nuclear devastation. And in the early years, was back when kaiju movies were made with the intent of being scary. Which in of itself could be used to look at Japan as they were dealing with all the fallout from the end of WWII (the American occupation, shift in government, and an even further Westernization of their culture). And the 60's also oversaw the creation of tokusatsu heroes like Ultraman, with an actual Hero rising to fight giant monsters (which could lead into the 70's and how that was the Golden Age of heroes for Japan with guys like Kamen Rider and Super Sentai).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh my god, the 80s in Japan would be perfect for Beast too, since that was the era of the various serial poisoners ( such as the Glico Morinaga case and the vending machine poisonings that killed a dozen people in 1985) that broke the image of Japan as being mosty safe and crime free and sent the nation into a panic. Maybe add hunter to it for the poisoner as slasher angle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T19:50:13-07:00","id":951455,"title":"","content":"I'd go with 70's Japan for a Beast era. Still plenty of kaiju to go around, with the benefit of a mine of Hero material. The backdrop that sells it for me though is the upswing in right wing extremism (the Mishima Incident being the most well known example) that showed the underlying cracks in the Yoshida Consensus and forced an uncomfortable confrontation with the legacy of Japan's past imperialism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-15T23:26:25-07:00","id":951518,"title":"","content":"What I'd also love would be a real crossover Era with two o more splats. We've had Eras with two splats, but they've been at their own. Just werewolf Vikings and Sin-Eaters vikings, not ho vikings werewolves and geist interacting among them.<br /> <br /> One obvious (someone suggested it in this thread) would be an Arturian crossover of mage and changeling, with both of them being involved in the Camelot court, and interacting and working together in its success (or its downfall).<br /> <br /> Another one could be a Mummy/Mage (and/or Werewolf) crossover during the Irem vs. Kir-En-Gi wars. It could be a good opportunity of creating an Iremite setting (as they did with Pangea), and given they fought against Kir-En-Gi mages, to include the mesopotamian mages o that time (if I remember correctly, the first mage societies of that region were Scelesti), and given that later Sumeria will be one of the focal points of Werewolves history, may be they could also be included). The main problem for all of this, is that may be it could be a setting too big for just one chapter of a new Dark Eras book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":247,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","user":"Uxas","date":". 08-16-2016, 02:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T00:42:31-07:00","id":951535,"title":"","content":"People mentioning kaiju Japan made me realize early 50's USSR could be great for Promethean, with the start of the Soviet nuclear program and some general mad science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T04:26:20-07:00","id":951598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daigotsu Max</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951535#post951535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People mentioning kaiju Japan made me realize early 50's USSR could be great for Promethean, with the start of the Soviet nuclear program and some general mad science.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Zeka would be pleased, even if there's only one or so of them at the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T18:51:04-07:00","id":952195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951518#post951518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'd also love would be a real crossover Era with two o more splats. We've had Eras with two splats, but they've been at their own. Just werewolf Vikings and Sin-Eaters vikings, not ho vikings werewolves and geist interacting among them.<br /> <br /> One obvious (someone suggested it in this thread) would be an Arturian crossover of mage and changeling, with both of them being involved in the Camelot court, and interacting and working together in its success (or its downfall).<br /> <br /> Another one could be a Mummy/Mage (and/or Werewolf) crossover during the Irem vs. Kir-En-Gi wars. It could be a good opportunity of creating an Iremite setting (as they did with Pangea), and given they fought against Kir-En-Gi mages, to include the mesopotamian mages o that time (if I remember correctly, the first mage societies of that region were Scelesti), and given that later Sumeria will be one of the focal points of Werewolves history, may be they could also be included). The main problem for all of this, is that may be it could be a setting too big for just one chapter of a new Dark Eras book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only problem with an Arthurian setting would be... when exactly would you set it? Because there's serious debate over whether or not Arthur existed, or if he is inspired by one or more figures who were active in England at the time. But let's assume that by &quot;Arthurian,&quot; we mean the period in which one of the &quot;King Arthur candidates&quot; was alive/active, which leaves us with a window anywhere between the 100s and the 500s; the time frame in which any historical figure who carries similarities to King Arthur was active. This would be a really fertile time, as it represents the Roman Empire from its height to its downfall; Roman and Britannic culture meeting and melding, and members of the different splats interacting from across the culture and splat gap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T19:17:43-07:00","id":952210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uxas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951518#post951518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'd also love would be a real crossover Era with two o more splats. We've had Eras with two splats, but they've been at their own. Just werewolf Vikings and Sin-Eaters vikings, not ho vikings werewolves and geist interacting among them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem there is that Geist was added onto the werewolf section, rather than it being created with the two concepts in mind. I believe the Promethean and Vampire Black Plague Dark Era are meant to have them more entwined, though this is just a guess. The Neolithic Werewolf and Mage does have a lot of overlap, with the fiction starting off with a mage 'hiring' a pack of werewolves.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:27:09-07:00","id":952348,"title":"","content":"The Mutapa era in the companion was a crossover from the start, so it intertwines mages and mummies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T23:54:52-07:00","id":952361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=952195#post952195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with an Arthurian setting would be... when exactly would you set it? Because there's serious debate over whether or not Arthur existed, or if he is inspired by one or more figures who were active in England at the time. But let's assume that by &quot;Arthurian,&quot; we mean the period in which one of the &quot;King Arthur candidates&quot; was alive/active, which leaves us with a window anywhere between the 100s and the 500s; the time frame in which any historical figure who carries similarities to King Arthur was active. This would be a really fertile time, as it represents the Roman Empire from its height to its downfall; Roman and Britannic culture meeting and melding, and members of the different splats interacting from across the culture and splat gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dave once said his Arthurian Dark Era would be set in Britain's anarchy period, where the lost kingdom of Camelot was the mythical 'Atlantis' - as in ruins of before, lost Artifacts, Merlin's archmastery legacy, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T01:35:08-07:00","id":952388,"title":"","content":"Kinda.<br /> <br /> The Arthurian World did exist (in some form, it was probably closer to earlier Dark Ages, Arthur laughing as he wrestles bears and smites men versions than after it got lancelotted and romantic fantasied) sometime in post-Roman Britain. It was the pet project of a welsh Silver Ladder Acanthus (and either the founder of or an early member of the Walkers in Mists Legacy) with the Shadow Name of Myrddin (or, in English, Merlin). He achieved archmastery, and his Noumenon, the great act of magic that made him Ascend, was to manipulate Fate to great and then doom the society he built, marking the Symbolism of Arcadia forever. Among the side effects was turning the astral anthropomorphism of Fate into Mordred.<br /> <br /> Then the Arcadian Exarchs deleted the whole thing from the timeline, and history became as we know it. Myrddin, safely Ascended as the very symbol of a cunning bastard, gave no shits.<br /> <br /> Tldr - it is a longstanding setting element of Mage, since Tome of the Watchtowers nearly ten years ago, that Merlin was a real mage, that the crystal cave was what he *wanted* (his ascension) and the fall of Camelot was entirely deliberate on his part. It predates Changeling as a gameline.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't set a Dark Era during it, anyway. The Anarchy era mentioned above would draw inspiration from things like Cadfael and the Pillars of the Earth, and be based on the last major conflict between the two Orders that would later merge to become the Mysterium. In a Britain falling apart, should mages stay hidden or attempt to guide Sleepers? Monastic Diamond mages fighting a war of ideals in the midst of a civil war.<br /> <br /> It's just that the mages of the setting would use their own context for &quot;Atlantean&quot; things, and be unable to tell them apart from the abandoned scaffolding of Myrddin's scheming. What if the civil war wakes the red and white dragons? What do the nearly-vanished children of Gog and Magog make of the chaos in the mortal realm?<br /> <br /> And does Myrddin, archetypal Jerkass Acanthus, see what's happening from the Supernal and decide to get involved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":20}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-17T08:14:00-07:00","id":952529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=952388#post952388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And does Myrddin, archetypal Jerkass Acanthus, see what's happening from the Supernal and decide to get involved?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a rhetorical question, right? Because I can't fathom a manipulative jerkass (let alone a Mage) <i>not</i> sticking their nose in a mess they caused.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T14:30:35-07:00","id":955176,"title":"","content":"Hm, I'm thinking of going through some of the Mage and Promethean DEs and homebrewing them to work with Transgression and The Lightning Chronicle. Not sure whether to include new Dark Eras in those projects or adapt the existing ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:38:18-07:00","id":958642,"title":"","content":"Wow! Hopefully this time I can pitch in for Dark Eras 2. I already read some of the chapters for Dark Eras and I have to say that I'm pleased with them. Anyways, there was a whole list of Eras that weren't picked and I would like to see them again for Dark Eras 2.<br /> <br /> Vampire: the Jazz Age. I really want to see Vidal and the other characters in this time. <br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Aztec Empire and Meiji period. I really loved the Aztec Empire for skin thieves and I really want to see werewolf in this Era. As for Meiji period I'm sold what atamajakki said.<br /> <br /> Mage: Maya civilization classic or post classic period<br /> <br /> Changeling: Any pre-columbian setting. (Just curious to see the courts in this time.)<br /> <br /> Geist: Wild West<br /> <br /> Mummy: Inca Empire <br /> <br /> Demon: Renaissance Italy sounds awesome <br /> <br /> Beast: 50s 60s Japan Kaiju. I'm definitely sold on this one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2360,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","user":"Cecoyotl","date":". 08-27-2016, 04:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2360-cecoyotl","name":"Cecoyotl","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2360_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T01:59:45-07:00","id":958645,"title":"","content":"<b>Mage</b> really needs early Roman Empire period, circa 20 BCE, with advent of Seers of Throne Order into being!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T05:24:09-07:00","id":958697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=951301#post951301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One I'd like to see is 1950's-60's Japan for Beast.<br /> <br /> This was the time of the Kaiju Golden Age for Japan. Which of course the first kaiju movie Godzilla (1954) was a metaphor for unchecked nuclear devastation. And in the early years, was back when kaiju movies were made with the intent of being scary. Which in of itself could be used to look at Japan as they were dealing with all the fallout from the end of WWII (the American occupation, shift in government, and an even further Westernization of their culture). And the 60's also oversaw the creation of tokusatsu heroes like Ultraman, with an actual Hero rising to fight giant monsters (which could lead into the 70's and how that was the Golden Age of heroes for Japan with guys like Kamen Rider and Super Sentai).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oddly, I actually had a pitch for the same period for Changeling. Literally using the Gentry as a kaiju story analogue. With the devastation of the war, so many people went missing. The Gentry would have run rampant. So, this would be a period where a lot of those captives were returning.<br /> <br /> This is partly because the period gets a solid mention in Changeling 2e. <br /> <br /> Then again, I'm a huge advocate of dual-game settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T10:49:57-07:00","id":958800,"title":"","content":"One of the most intriguing tidbits from Beast was the blurb on Bombay Beach and the thing slumbering under the Salton Sea. I'm very curious to know what it is, how it got there... and when. The book mentions that it's seen the Salton Sea expand and contract many times over the ages. Stone Age Beast?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T13:08:03-07:00","id":958859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=945819#post945819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Someone else had proposed a Bronze Age Collapse setting for Beast, which I love but know nothing about).</div> </div> </div> </div>That was me. I think it's a good choice because it seems like the last point in (Mediterranean) history where Beasts where relevant. Civilizations had been growing stronger and begun replacing primal fears with more modern fears, and then it all started falling apart. It must have been very validating for Beasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T14:20:52-07:00","id":958888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenorath</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=958859#post958859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was me. I think it's a good choice because it seems like the last point in (Mediterranean) history where Beasts where relevant. Civilizations had been growing stronger and begun replacing primal fears with more modern fears, and then it all started falling apart. It must have been very validating for Beasts.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say nothing of how much fun it would be to play Beasts whose Horrors take the shapes of the great monsters of Greek myth.<br /> <br /> Have I already talked about my idea for Greek Beast/Deviant crossover, or did I imagine that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T17:03:26-07:00","id":958962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=958888#post958888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To say nothing of how much fun it would be to play Beasts whose Horrors take the shapes of the great monsters of Greek myth.<br /> <br /> Have I already talked about my idea for Greek Beast/Deviant crossover, or did I imagine that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the quote is from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/477-xenorath","name":"Xenorath","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"169"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T17:59:27-07:00","id":958983,"title":"","content":"70s San Francisco Bay big three (vampire, werewolf and mage), because as awesome as New York in the 70s was for werewolf, all the really crazy shit happened on the west coast that decade and the magi would be trying to see how the insanity ties into the mystery of Emperor Norton's Legacy and the uratha would be desperately trying to keep the shadow from shattering from the conflicts between the various ideologies and the vampire section would show more the history of The Mission and it's kindred, from a less Daeva centric position than their clanbook had. For instance, I imagine the nos politics surrounding the BART subway connecting the various cites of the bay being built would be brutal and the Ventrue would probably have something to say about the brainwashing of Patty Hearst, even if they weren't involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T19:31:45-07:00","id":959031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=958888#post958888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To say nothing of how much fun it would be to play Beasts whose Horrors take the shapes of the great monsters of Greek myth.<br /> <br /> Have I already talked about my idea for Greek Beast/Deviant crossover, or did I imagine that?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know where the Beast Player's Guide stands, but I really hope that at some point, we get some sort of z-splat to create characters whose Horrors are/were the inspiration from real-world monsters and creatures.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:28:36-07:00","id":959102,"title":"","content":"As it happens, I can think of only two time periods I'd like to explore that haven't already been mentioned: The British Raj, and Hawai'i up to and including the arrival of Captain Cook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:44:34-07:00","id":959107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cecoyotl</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=958642#post958642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changeling: Any pre-columbian setting. (Just curious to see the courts in this time.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a lot easier with 2E than before. I definitely want pre-columbian settings, but I'm not hung up on Changeling needing to be one, since 2E Courts are meant to be &quot;build your own&quot; anyway. Not to say I'm AGAINST a pre-columbian Changeling setting or anything! It could be very cool.<br /> <br /> My #1 pitch for a pre-columbian era would be Hunter at the birth of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois Confederacy).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T22:47:14-07:00","id":959108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=959102#post959102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The British Raj</div> </div> </div> </div>Any reason you're more inclined to go Raj (i.e. post-1857) than going pre-Mutiny, with the East India Company, (accurate) thuggee, rise of the rebellion, etc?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T23:10:12-07:00","id":959115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=959102#post959102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As it happens, I can think of only two time periods I'd like to explore that haven't already been mentioned: The British Raj, and Hawai'i up to and including the arrival of Captain Cook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Polynesian anything could use a lot more love. I'm glad it's showing up in Scion, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T06:49:45-07:00","id":959209,"title":"","content":"Sengoku Jidai Japan, American Civil War, Russia in the last decades/years of the empire, British Raj, Rome in the last days of the republic, Age of Discovery Central America.<br /> <br /> And, as a love-letter to the V:tM game that made me truly appreciate it thanks to Onyx Path's very own Matthew Dawkins, a Vampire Dark Era set in Berlin set right before and after the Wall came down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":6498,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","user":"Haberdasher","date":". 08-28-2016, 09:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-28T16:20:25-07:00","id":959557,"title":"","content":"How about Samarkand during the reign of Timur? I was thinking Promethean, since Timur gathered the best artisans and craftsman from across the empire to rebuild the city and create great works of art. It seems like an environment where new Prometheans would be born. Also, with Mongol, Turkish, and Persian cultures all mixing to make something new, it seems like a neat metaphor for a Promethean's quest to build their own identities. Timur spent the entirety of his reign building and rebuilding the city. The constant change could have an effect on the balance of Azoth and Flux, such that Disquiet and Wastelands might be milder for the moment, making it easier for Prometheans to stay here and interact with people. Of course, things unbalanced eventually must shift the other way. Lurking in the future is the death of Timur and the violent struggle for succession which will follow. For the moment, though, Samarkand is a peaceful respite on their Pilgrimage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T11:37:09-07:00","id":959926,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see Somalia at the hight of piracy. It would be a crossover game between Hunter (well, just Task Force: VALKARIE), Changeling and Gesit. Each group would be convinced they're in a completely different genre.<ul><li>The Changelings think they're in a swashbuckling pirate story. More than anything they're just here to have fun and have a very Spring Court vibe. They're more interested in singing sea shanties and drinking rum than actually being pirates, and when they raid a cruise liner they're more interested in flirting with the passengers than taking their jewellery. This is of course powering the Freehold Bulwark.</li> <li>The Sin Eaters think they're in an epic (that is, the film style called <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epic_film\" target=\"_blank\">epics</a>) in which the ghosts of Somalia's past is called up from the underworld; old wrongs are put right, forgotten history is remembered, and at the end of it Somalia will rise above the legacy of colonialism to forge a new national identity that can stand in the modern world as equals.</li> <li>Meanwhile Task Force: VALKARIE think they're in, well, a game of Hunter the Vigil focused on TF:V. Where strange and horrific monsters with alien thought patterns and unknowable motives prey upon humanity (and their cargo ships) and humanity must rise to the challenge with military discipline.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> (You could throw in Leviathans; who'd think they're basically in Game of Thrones - but if this is an offical product Leviathans are not going to happen)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T21:04:01-07:00","id":960211,"title":"","content":"Don't know if it's been said already, but Australia in the 1930-40's for Changeling could be rather interesting considering the horrific &quot;Stolen Generation&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:08:05-07:00","id":961296,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=959108#post959108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any reason you're more inclined to go Raj (i.e. post-1857) than going pre-Mutiny, with the East India Company, (accurate) thuggee, rise of the rebellion, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div>Truth be told, I don't know that much about pre-Raj India. I just thought it was an interesting period of contrasts, and a chapter on it could provide an interesting examination of contemporary Indian culture, not to mention the British Colonial &quot;Great White Hunter&quot; shtick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:39:20-07:00","id":961306,"title":"","content":"I think that if Promethean is going to signal that it needs a WW1 setting by mentioning a Lineage from the time, we might as well make it a crossover with Changeling. CtL has an easy reading as a PTSD metaphor, but is usually seen from an abuse survivor perspective; shifting that to struggles of combat veterans returning home from a living hell (often missing pieces of themselves) to a world they barely remember that is made uncomfortable by their presence and add in the tragic poetry produced by the Lost Generation (coincidence in naming?) and you have something really interesting there. I know Ruins of Empire touched on this somewhat, but only in the wider global context and from an outsider perspective; this would be more about the normal men in the trenches and their struggles once the fighting ends. <br /> <br /> If you want to get real crazy with it, use this as an excuse to update that one poisoner Vampire Bloodline from Ypres to 2e and make it a triple crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T18:44:50-07:00","id":961329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=960211#post960211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't know if it's been said already, but Australia in the 1930-40's for Changeling could be rather interesting considering the horrific &amp;quot;Stolen Generation&amp;quot; situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gut reaction is 'please be very, very careful'. There are still many victims of the stolen generations alive today, and this would have to be treated incredibly sensitively. I can see how it could be done, but (in a world where I was involved with this if it were a thing) I'd want to sit down with the developers and draw the structure and Changeling parallels in a considered manner before putting fingers to keyboard.<br /> <br /> I know victims of this period and their descendants. And yes, I acknowledge that I am someone who has written about the stolen generation in an OPP product. I believe we got the balance right in that one.<br /> <br /> To turn this into something more positive than a call for care - milo v3, what aspects of this era do you think would be particularly interesting?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T20:02:01-07:00","id":961370,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see:<br /> -The Caliphate of Cordoba, for Mage<br /> -Kublai Khan's empire, for Hunter<br /> -The 14th century Empire of Mali, for Geist<br /> -Justinian I &amp; Theodora's Byzantine Empire, for Vampire<br /> -The Anglo-Zulu War for Werewolf<br /> -King Narai's Ayuttha Kingdom for Changeling<br /> -Ivan the Terrible's Russia for Beast<br /> -Nebuchadnezzar's Babylon, for Demon","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T00:31:55-07:00","id":962147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=961329#post961329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gut reaction is 'please be very, very careful'. There are still many victims of the stolen generations alive today, and this would have to be treated incredibly sensitively. I can see how it could be done, but (in a world where I was involved with this if it were a thing) I'd want to sit down with the developers and draw the structure and Changeling parallels in a considered manner before putting fingers to keyboard.<br /> <br /> I know victims of this period and their descendants. And yes, I acknowledge that I am someone who has written about the stolen generation in an OPP product. I believe we got the balance right in that one.<br /> <br /> To turn this into something more positive than a call for care - milo v3, what aspects of this era do you think would be particularly interesting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I do definitely agree that the writers would have to be very very careful (to the extent where I actually thought about it 3 days before my post, thinking it might be too volatile), and consideration would have to be made on which parallels you are willing to touch. One aspect that I feel would be interesting to see (beyond just the base kidnapping by gentry and changing people forever in a traumatic and horrific manner), would be that changeling has an immense focus on folk-lore/fairytales/myth, and that period is one where the stories of a country suddenly stop being able to be passed to their children. Sort of a reverse of the Grim dark era, instead of stories suddenly becoming available to an immense amount of people, story and tradition are torn away.<br /> <br /> In addition, during those times there were other events such as the great depression having effects like changing the countries chief economy from agriculture to manufacturing (so people are moving away from bushlands and places more tied to folklore), and the unemployment rate being between 25% and 29% (depending on the source) so there'd be an immense amount of vulnerable people for gentry and hobgoblins to pray upon (not just kidnapping-wise, but also in that they can promise them work or a good life rather than dying in the streets).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 09-02-2016, 03:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T23:09:45-07:00","id":962716,"title":"","content":"90s or 00s Demon could potentially be fun. I just finished rereading Hippo Eats Dwarf, and it reminded me that the bizarre culture of the early internet is ripe for a really surreal, out-there Demon or GMC story. It's hard not to read HED and not kind of think to yourself &quot;holy shit, this is when we broke reality&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T11:28:56-07:00","id":963294,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in seeing what &quot;wild card&quot; Dark Eras get in this time- really unexpected stuff, like the Neolithic era was.<br /> <br /> And of course, I'd be over the moon if we got a future or alternate history Dark Era.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-04-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T13:04:03-07:00","id":963349,"title":"","content":"Poking my head back here to suggest an Egyptian Dark Era during Akhenaten's reign. The Mekhet clan book depicted him as a Witch King, and Dark Eras' To the Strongest made mention of an Aten Heresy in the Weret-Hekau section.<br /> <br /> That said, perhaps this could be a Mage/Vampire crossover?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T13:48:08-07:00","id":963366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=962716#post962716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">90s or 00s Demon could potentially be fun. I just finished rereading Hippo Eats Dwarf, and it reminded me that the bizarre culture of the early internet is ripe for a really surreal, out-there Demon or GMC story. It's hard not to read HED and not kind of think to yourself &quot;holy shit, this is when we broke reality&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suggested Mage for the dot-com bubble due to the theme of hubris and utopia that didn't happen. Maybe a shared setting would be good for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:07:42-07:00","id":963380,"title":"","content":"That could be fun RE Lemuria, especially if you picked the dot-com bubble to mark their renaissance, when they stopped just being weirdo steampunks and atompunks and started picking up some more modern ideologies and influences, and started to recover from the war. You could get a lot from how that era basically made the basic Lemurian concept of &quot;we were cheated out of the future we deserved&quot; more mainstream.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's for Transgression. For Awakening, 2e pushes the whole mystery thing more than hubris or utopia as themes, so if I were doing it for Awakening I'd keep the tone of the Demon section and have the central conflict he about people fighting to understand how the world works suddenly facing a massive upheaval in the fundamental way people interact with each other. <br /> <br /> Though I think it would work best as a Demon/Mortals era. And it could be early 2000s, but Eternal September might also be a fun focal point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-04-2016, 05:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:43:08-07:00","id":963393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963349#post963349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poking my head back here to suggest an Egyptian Dark Era during Akhenaten's reign. The Mekhet clan book depicted him as a Witch King, and Dark Eras' To the Strongest made mention of an Aten Heresy in the Weret-Hekau section.<br /> <br /> That said, perhaps this could be a Mage/Vampire crossover?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that in Ancient Mysteries?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T14:45:11-07:00","id":963395,"title":"","content":"It was in the Mekhet clanbook, but it was strongly insinuated to be Mekhet using Dominate and blood bondage to have scribes change their descriptions of how things really were.<br /> <br /> Referenced from other site, source edited it to be SFW, not me.<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.warosu.org/data/tg/img/0331/52/1404346877954.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"https://i.warosu.org/data/tg/img/0331/52/1404346946661.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 09-04-2016, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T15:00:53-07:00","id":963404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963380#post963380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be fun RE Lemuria, especially if you picked the dot-com bubble to mark their renaissance, when they stopped just being weirdo steampunks and atompunks and started picking up some more modern ideologies and influences, and started to recover from the war. You could get a lot from how that era basically made the basic Lemurian concept of &quot;we were cheated out of the future we deserved&quot; more mainstream.<br /> <br /> Of course, that's for Transgression. For Awakening, 2e pushes the whole mystery thing more than hubris or utopia as themes, so if I were doing it for Awakening I'd keep the tone of the Demon section and have the central conflict he about people fighting to understand how the world works suddenly facing a massive upheaval in the fundamental way people interact with each other.<br /> <br /> Though I think it would work best as a Demon/Mortals era. And it could be early 2000s, but Eternal September might also be a fun focal point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some of SJgames' material from the 90s has a recurring theme of how computers might as well be magic to many of the people who rely on them everyday, I imagine that mage could benefit from that inspiration. In particular, the conspiratorial history of computers in those sidebars from chapter 3 of GURPS Y2K seems like the CofD magi could get some fun from it, as they would from anything involving Alister Crowley, British intelligence, Ian Fleming, Nostradamus (ask me about my theory that his quatrains predict multiple likely futures rather than a single future set in stone sometime, it's a real trip.), Issac Newton's feud with Leibniz, Plato himself and Mesopotamian mythology.<br /> <br /> Seriously, the idea that the seers of the throne had been suppressing computer tech for millennia only to catastrophically fail in the 90s, following computers becoming non-secret knowledge due to Babbage seems like a fun basis for a dark era shared with demon.<br /> <br /> In your setting, though, I imagine the business models of the failed dotcoms were financial wonders that fell apart when looked at too closely.<br /> <br /> Also, my novel series features an ancient prophecy that refers to the Eternal September as one of it's signs, but calls it the Autumn Unending. The heroes get a bit confused by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-04-2016, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T15:25:23-07:00","id":963417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963393#post963393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't that in Ancient Mysteries?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ancient Mysteries has Ramesses the Great, I believe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/627-mr-innes","name":"Mr Innes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"65"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T19:31:25-07:00","id":963487,"title":"","content":"A period during the colonization of the Americas for Mummy would be great, because you get the chance to be among the first Arisen to arrive there.<br /> <br /> I forget who it is who has the &quot;Dark Eras: Electroweak Epoch&quot; sig, but that could actually work for Genius or Mage...the only good thing about the wait for this is that I don't have to rush to get the existing Dark Eras updated for Transgression and TLC (if it's even needed, tbh. DE stuff tends not to need much modification). <br /> <br /> Hmmmm, thinking about those two projects going forward...does anyone have any ideas for a Mage: The Transgression era? The obvious one, though, is to just do The War in the middle of the twentieth century between the Peerage and Lemuria. I might actually do that an include it with the Player's Guide. <br /> <br /> And I'm not seeing many Promethean suggestions, which is a shame but understandable. On the topic of future/alternate history Dark Eras, though, I proposed &quot;Art Deco Dieselpunk Retro-Future Promethean&quot; as an Era based on Metropolis, Janelle Monae, and the Protomen. Speaking of, that's planned for the Lightning Chronicle Guide too. I might stick the updated Handful of Dust there, but I'm not that fond of it. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a>, would you mind if I wrote up your proposed 1950s Promethean setting for TLC? If yes, I'll credit you for the concept in whatever way you want.<br /> <br /> And this is only somewhat related to the thread topic, but dear god I would be ecstatic to see anything from Mirrors show up again, and having a post-apocalyptic or Infinite Macabre Dark Era would be a super cool way to do that. So there's another question- if DE2 was going to have post-apocalypse, Infinite Macabre, and Bleeding Edge as Eras, which would you give to which gameline? Personally, I'd do Post-Apoc Vampire/Werewolf, Infinite Macabre Beast/Demon, and Bleeding Edge Promethean/Deviant.<br /> <br /> ...argh, if I wasn't writing so much other stuff right now I'd probably be making plans to actually write up those six ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 09-04-2016, 10:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T20:07:18-07:00","id":963498,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Gecko, this is the last time I'm warning you to stop bringing up fan projects in threads not specifically devoted to them. The next time they are brought up outside of a dedicated thread your posting privileges will be suspended.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T03:19:15-07:00","id":963616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963393#post963393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't that in Ancient Mysteries?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963395#post963395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was in the Mekhet clanbook, but it was strongly insinuated to be Mekhet using Dominate and blood bondage to have scribes change their descriptions of how things really were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still, there's a lot of room for creativity given how Akhenaten has been more or less stricken from Egyptian records.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T08:20:17-07:00","id":963700,"title":"","content":"A Hunter/Changeling crossover era during the height of the UFO craze could be very interesting. Maybe something situated in the American Southwest that plays into the beauty and strangeness of the desert. Reports of mysterious lights in the sky signal the beginnings of Project FORT and Network Zero. A startling number of people are claiming to have been abducted by aliens, some of whom are telling the truth, but not in the way they think. New stories are creating new types of Gentry with new ways of preying on the mortal populace. Will TFV work with the local Freeholds, or are the barriers for effective communication too high? And what to do about those fringe societies who actively <i>want</i> to be taken away by extraterrestrials? More than one alien cult is playing with forces they barely understand. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T14:42:58-07:00","id":963918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963700#post963700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Hunter/Changeling crossover era during the height of the UFO craze could be very interesting. Maybe something situated in the American Southwest that plays into the beauty and strangeness of the desert. Reports of mysterious lights in the sky signal the beginnings of Project FORT and Network Zero. A startling number of people are claiming to have been abducted by aliens, some of whom are telling the truth, but not in the way they think. New stories are creating new types of Gentry with new ways of preying on the mortal populace. Will TFV work with the local Freeholds, or are the barriers for effective communication too high? And what to do about those fringe societies who actively <i>want</i> to be taken away by extraterrestrials? More than one alien cult is playing with forces they barely understand. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Go with Vegas, which is in its post-WW2 boom with gangsters and atomic testing at the nearby Nevada Test Range (the tests were a tourist draw). I've always thought that Vegas was the perfect Changeling setting with desperate people willing to make deals and gamble their souls for what they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T15:17:13-07:00","id":963939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963918#post963918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go with Vegas, which is in its post-WW2 boom with gangsters and atomic testing at the nearby Nevada Test Range (the tests were a tourist draw). I've always thought that Vegas was the perfect Changeling setting with desperate people willing to make deals and gamble their souls for what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want a jumping off point, Ken Hite did a Ken Writes About Stuff focused on 1968 Vegas as a setting for whatever game you please. It touches on both the criminal history and some neat occult stuff as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T06:35:36-07:00","id":964261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963918#post963918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Go with Vegas, which is in its post-WW2 boom with gangsters and atomic testing at the nearby Nevada Test Range (the tests were a tourist draw). I've always thought that Vegas was the perfect Changeling setting with desperate people willing to make deals and gamble their souls for what they want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vegas as a Changeling/Demon Crossover chapter? Both have the deal-making down. I guess the hardest part is figuring out which is which when cutting a deal.<br /> <br /> ...And now I have the mental image of a Changeling and Demon duo making rounds and getting people to sign contracts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T10:23:56-07:00","id":964370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=963939#post963939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a jumping off point, Ken Hite did a Ken Writes About Stuff focused on 1968 Vegas as a setting for whatever game you please. It touches on both the criminal history and some neat occult stuff as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I've been kinda obsessed with the occult side of Vegas since reading Last Call. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T14:45:38-07:00","id":964543,"title":"","content":"I think I've said this elsewhere, but I think 1930s Shanghai (under Japanese occupation) makes a fantastic &quot;and the kitchen sink&quot; crossover setting. This is a world where Triad gangsters, White Russian expats, Imperial Japanese soldiers, Nazi spies, and Western playboys with more money than sense all fight, mingle, and die under the glittering neon lights; with the mortal situation already so volatile, adding vampires and mummies barely even registers as odd. You could either play it as a glamorous noir story as the last gasp of an era crushed by foreign oppression or as high-flying, bad guy-punching action in the streets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T19:44:45-07:00","id":966542,"title":"","content":"Three words: Kowloon Walled City. I'd probably make it Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:31:40-07:00","id":966560,"title":"","content":"I would like to see a post great war Europe setting for changeling probably in Paris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:02:52-07:00","id":966646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=966542#post966542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three words: Kowloon Walled City. I'd probably make it Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what would the Kindred <i>possibly</i> want in a city where missing people aren't noticed and many streets go untouched by sunlight, hmm?<br /> <br /> I'd love to see 1980s Kowloon as a Vampire/Geist crossover, with the killers and those who aid the dead fighting for the souls of those in the Walled City.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=966560#post966560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see a post great war Europe setting for changeling probably in Paris.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tie this into the birth of the Surrealist art movement and I'm sold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T23:09:41-07:00","id":966649,"title":"","content":"You know what I said about how OP could put out five more Dark Eras books without running out of ideas? This thread is the proof. Any idea here could work out. <br /> <br /> Kowloon would be especially cool because it's such a confined area, so you have the &quot;local&quot; atmosphere of ChroD boiled down to an extreme. Lex mentioned this, but it's just so perfect- you have this bizarre labyrinth tower of crime, and it actually existed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T01:02:38-07:00","id":966671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=966649#post966649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know what I said about how OP could put out five more Dark Eras books without running out of ideas? This thread is the proof. Any idea here could work out. <br /> <br /> Kowloon would be especially cool because it's such a confined area, so you have the &amp;quot;local&amp;quot; atmosphere of ChroD boiled down to an extreme. Lex mentioned this, but it's just so perfect- you have this bizarre labyrinth tower of crime, and it actually existed!</div> </div> </div> </div>And I would back five more Dark Eras kickstarters. It's the easiest way I can imagine making sure each line gets new content each year without doing supplements for every game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T05:08:03-07:00","id":966714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/945788-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-dark-eras-2?p=966671#post966671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And I would back five more Dark Eras kickstarters. It's the easiest way I can imagine making sure each line gets new content each year without doing supplements for every game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially since they sneak new material mechanics into the chapters.<br /> <br /> Heck, after 5 DEs, they could even do Compilation books containing only one game-line's Dark Eras to date and their associated expansion content without actually having to write anything new (for the people that missed the previous Kickstarters). It would be like Sothis Ascends for every line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:03:58-07:00","id":967136,"title":"","content":"What would be a good historical setting to have Slasher content in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:06:27-07:00","id":967137,"title":"","content":"Some period of war or where death is common and the difference would be hard to tell between a slasher and a 'regular' person at first glance but would be very clearly obvious if given a fuller picture of the slasher's activities providing they had time to grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T21:10:04-07:00","id":967138,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, do the 80s, and have it be one big tribute to slasher movies, Hotline Miami, and the outrun aesthetic in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:14:15-07:00","id":967173,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, I'm sure Whitechapel in the CofD was a damn sight more messy than it was in reality after Saucy Jack did his work; it was probably swarming with copycat Rippers, either emboldened by such public murders or possessed by a memetic need to slaughter the innocent from some alien outside force (Murder-Claimed, goetic creature of Victorian sensibility driven mad, frenzied draugr frantically hunted by those who keep the Masquerade, bloody Banisher with an unknown or unknowable scheme, etc etc etc)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-10T22:27:08-07:00","id":967177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <di